  "english": "But if it happens to fall during the Fast of Catechumens [Yarajavorats],\nor during the Great Lent, on February 13, at the Midday Hour:\nthey shall say the three \"Have Mercy\" [Oghormya] hymns according to the order of the day,\nand they shall read the Scripture [books] of the day;\nthey shall say the \"For the Souls\" [Hogvots] prayer and be dismissed,\nomitting [the prayers] \"Bow Down [Your Ear]\" (Khonarhetso) and \"Save [Us]\" (Apretso).\nThen in the evening, \"Bow Down [Your Ear]\" (Khonarhetso) and \"Save [Us]\" (Apretso) and so on, according to the above-written instruction.\nAnd during the night, which is February 14,\nthere is a vigil with services and psalms.\nAnd the Holy Sacrament is placed upon a table in the chancel;\nand all, having vested, shall come into the chancel,\nand they shall say the processional [hetevak] hymn in Tone 3 [gd]: \"Who became incarnate from the Virgin\" (Marmnatsyald i kusen).\nAnd the Blessing [Orhnutiun] hymn in Tone 4 [dad]: \"Today, without beginning\" (Aysor anskzbnakan).\nAlleluia. \"Blessed is He who comes\" and \"The Lord our God.\"\nAnd then they shall read the four Gospels in the four corners of the church.\n\nThe first Gospel they shall read facing the East.\nHymn, Tone 1 [ats]: \"Who became incarnate\" (Marmnatsyald), \"Rejoice greatly\" (Urakh ler yoyzh), \"Image-sharing\" (Patkerakits).\nAfter which: \"Stand [firm]\" (Ortiu). Gospel according to Matthew 5:17–20: \"Do not think that...\" to \"...into the kingdom of heaven.\"\n\nThe second facing the West side.\nHymn, Tone 4 [dz]: \"Today, without beginning\" (Aysor anskzbnakan), \"Today having come to the temple\" (Aysor i tacharn ekial).\nAfter which: \"Stand [firm]\" (Ortiu). Gospel according to Mark 13:32–37: \"But about that day...\" to \"...keep watch.\"\n\nThe third facing the South side.\nHymn, Tone 4 [dz]: \"Light from Light\" (Loys i lusoy), \"You who [by] Spirit\" (Zkez vor hogi).\nAfter which: \"Stand [firm]\" (Ortiu). Gospel according to Luke 12:49–59: \"I came to bring fire...\" to \"...the very last penny.\"\n\nAnd the fourth facing the North side.\nHymn, Tone 4 [ek]: \"Today in the temple\" (Aysor i tacharn), \"In the beginning was the Word\" (I skzbane bann).\nAfter which: \"Stand [firm]\" (Ortiu). Gospel according to John 1:1–17: \"In the beginning was the Word...\" to \"...came through Christ.\"\n\nAfter which, hymn, Tone 2 [bk]: \"At the coming of the Lord\" (I galstean tearn).\nAnd then coming into the chancel they shall say the \"Fathers\" [Harts] hymn with its canons.\nAnd if it happens on a Sunday,\nread the Myrrhbearers [Yughaberits] Gospel.\nSong: \"Sun of Justice\" (Aregakn ardarutean).\nLitany: \"Holy Mother\" (Mayr surb). \"Holy God.\"",
